hat follow-up ticket actually exists/was created.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f94da2157afd2cb62","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Accepted scope limits (documented, follow-up filed as discovered_from this story)'","norm_id":"nfccff424aa7ea061","priority":0.7143,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Story closes with the deferred trio undocumented in a tracked follow-up, silently losing the deferral."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'A discovered_from follow-up ticket exists covering check_ac/quality_check/declare_no_file_impact cross-session warnings (checked by show_ticket on the follow-up id), and docs/mcp-reference.md names the deferred trio (grep).'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the pre-mutation cross_session_warning_for call is wrapped fail-safe (swallow exceptions -> warning None) so a detector/state/config read failure can never abort the underlying write or transition, mirroring _push_status()'s 'must never fail a completed write' guard.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.27,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["cross_session_warning_for does live reads: 'state = show_ticket(...); acting = resolve_session_id(); config = load_config(...)' (_commands/cross_session.py:39-41), any of which can raise","The sibling advisory helper is deliberately fail-safe: '_push_status()... except Exception: ... a status read must never fail a completed write' (_mcp_writes.py:54-57), and runs AFTER the write","The plan's chosen pre-mutation ordering means a detector exception aborts the op before rebar.<op>() runs, widening blast radius beyond the advisory itself"],"finding":"The plan computes cross_session_warning_for BEFORE the mutation but does not specify failure handling for that call; because it precedes rebar.<op>(), an exception from the detector (its internal show_ticket / load_config / resolve_session_id reads on corrupt/locked/absent state or bad config) would abort the entire write or transition — converting a purely-advisory field into a hard failure of the primary operation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f81417a74e70c74da","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach § 'Compute the warning BEFORE the underlying mutation runs'","norm_id":"n4fd8441f933f64f2","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A held ticket's state file is briefly locked/partially-written when a write handler runs; the pre-mutation detector call raises and the comment/edit/transition fails even though the mutation would have succeeded","A malformed warnings.cross_session config makes load_config raise, failing every single-ticket write instead of silently skipping the advisory"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In _ack / the transition and reopen handlers, wrap the cross_session_warning_for(...) call in try/except Exception returning None (as _push_status does), and add a test that forces the detector to raise and asserts the mutation still applies and cross_session_warning is None.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the fallback when `cross_session_warning_for` raises during the pre-mutation computation (e.g. swallow the exception and treat the warning as `None`, mirroring `_push_status`'s try/except), so an advisory failure never aborts the underlying single-ticket op.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.37,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'each handler calls `cross_session_warning_for` first (reading the live holder), then performs `rebar.<op>(...)`'","`cross_session_warning_for` (src/rebar/_commands/cross_session.py:33-43) composes show_ticket, resolve_session_id and load_config — real reads that can raise.","The analogous existing advisory guards itself: `_push_status` (src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:54-57) wraps its read in try/except because 'a status read must never fail a completed write' — the plan does not extend this guarantee to the cross-session computation, and running it pre-mutation makes an unguarded raise abort the op."],"finding":"The plan does not specify a fallback when the pre-mutation advisory computation (`cross_session_warning_for`, which does live show_ticket / resolve_session_id / load_config reads) raises. Because the plan mandates computing it BEFORE `rebar.<op>(...)`, an exception in the advisory would abort the underlying operation entirely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1d97aa0d6f8ab141","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Compute the warning BEFORE the underlying mutation runs.'","norm_id":"n0e3cabe9a40133d8","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Config file transiently unreadable/corrupt, or the ticket-state read raises during warning computation, on a write/read that would otherwise succeed."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State that the handler wraps the pre-mutation `cross_session_warning_for` call in a best-effort guard (try/except -> None), matching `_push_status`, so a failed advisory computation degrades to silence rather than failing the write/read/transition.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","